1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:01,433
<i> It's a clear sign...</i>

2
00:00:01,567 --> 00:00:03,367
<i> that someone saw me with Ramo.</i>

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,933
<i> But we saw something too.</i>

4
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:06,900
<i> We're looking for a woman.</i>

5
00:00:07,033 --> 00:00:08,400
<i> Then why did your uncle ask</i>

6
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:09,967
<i> if they had a female employe?</i>

7
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:10,967
<i>You didn't tell anyone else,
right?</i>

8
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:11,967
<i> Of course not.</i>

9
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:12,767
<i> How about you?</i>

10
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:13,900
<i> Of course not either.</i>

11
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:15,633
<i> Maybe we can talk to the doctr</i>

12
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:17,067
<i> about increasing mommy's dosag?</i>

13
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,133
<i> Mommy's dosage is already hig.</i>

14
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:20,400
<i> She's still in pain.</i>

15
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:21,800
<i> She's always in pain.</i>

16
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:24,000
<i> They've already traced the CCV
from the office.</i>

17
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:26,167
<i> We'll track that woman down.</i>

18
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,667
<i>Mister, at the next corner,
make a right turn.</i>

19
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,267
<i> On the day Ramon disappeare,</i>

20
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,867
<i> he left something with me.</i>

21
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,867
<i> He said...</i>

22
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,533
<i>that if anything
bad happened to him,</i>

23
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:37,200
<i>I should give it
to Miguel Delgado.</i>

24
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:39,733
<i> - What did you say?
- Your wife and child left yo?</i>

25
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:40,667
<i> Loser!</i>

26
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:45,067
<i> So who's the loser now, huh?</i>

27
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,700
<i>Joey, why are you only comig
home now?</i>

28
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:48,733
<i> I just had to stop by somewher.</i>

29
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:12,867
<i> Hi, fellow Saludos!</i>

30
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,633
<i>Today, we're here
at Bolagos National High School.</i>

31
00:01:15,767 --> 00:01:17,867
<i>Of course, I'm with
my very demure,</i>

32
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,333
<i>very mindful,
and very cutesy mom...</i>

33
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:47,067
Joey.

34
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,100
Mom.

35
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,067
Joey...

36
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,367
What are you peeking at there?

37
00:01:53,067 --> 00:01:54,000
Oh, nothing.

38
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:54,867
Oh...

39
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:57,667
It's just that dad taught me
to always be alert...

40
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,767
ever since I started
boarding on my own.

41
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:04,100
Sorry, Mom.

42
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:08,467
You don't have anything
to be sorry about, Joey.

43
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,533
You know, I'm actually happy.

44
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:14,133
Because even if
it's just the two of us here,

45
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,500
I still feel very safe....

46
00:02:17,633 --> 00:02:19,400
because of my brave daughter.

47
00:02:20,233 --> 00:02:21,767
Of course, Mom.

48
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,400
Even if gad isn't with us,

49
00:02:23,533 --> 00:02:25,733
I won't leave you.

50
00:02:25,867 --> 00:02:28,167
I won't let anything
happen to you.

51
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:34,267
You know, I should be the one
saying that to you.

52
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,867
Come on, eat now, okay?

53
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:38,800
Okay.

54
00:02:38,933 --> 00:02:40,567
- I'll heat up the soup.
- Okay.

55
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:41,933
This won't take long.

56
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,900
Major Delgado!

57
00:03:00,233 --> 00:03:01,433
Get that away.

58
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:04,867
Sir, they started it, Sir.

59
00:03:05,767 --> 00:03:08,467
You're not in a position
to retaliate, Major Delgado.

60
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:10,967
Just because you're suspended...

61
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,233
doesn't mean you won't follow
the Code of Conduct.

62
00:03:13,367 --> 00:03:15,767
Don't add more offenses
to your record.

63
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,233
Or else...

64
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:20,300
You might never return
to the service.

65
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:22,233
There's nothing left
for me to return to, Chief.

66
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,800
We've known each other
a long time,

67
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:26,333
and I've been in the service
for decades.

68
00:03:27,467 --> 00:03:29,267
My name is clean.

69
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:31,000
I have no record.

70
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:33,733
But because of one accusation

71
00:03:33,867 --> 00:03:35,600
with no evidence,

72
00:03:35,733 --> 00:03:36,900
you threw me under the bus.

73
00:03:37,033 --> 00:03:39,400
And these idiots
disrespected me.

74
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,100
Miguel, that's enough, buddy.

75
00:03:42,233 --> 00:03:44,267
Watch your words.

76
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:46,867
I just feel sorry for you,

77
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:49,967
but I won't tolerate disrespect.

78
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:52,200
Keep your pity.

79
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,733
Miguel!

80
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,867
Buddy!

81
00:04:10,533 --> 00:04:12,033
What is this?

82
00:04:13,267 --> 00:04:14,333
I don't know either.

83
00:04:14,467 --> 00:04:17,700
Maybe only the two
of them understand Miguel?

84
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:36,267
You know, I think
I'm really getting paranoid.

85
00:04:37,533 --> 00:04:39,367
I really feel like
I have a stalker.

86
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:40,633
Earlier, that black car,

87
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:42,167
I thought it was following me.

88
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:43,367
But it wasn't.

89
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,833
Am I overreacting?

90
00:04:46,267 --> 00:04:47,633
You're just implying something.

91
00:04:48,467 --> 00:04:49,833
You want me to escort you
to and from school

92
00:04:49,967 --> 00:04:51,133
so you're sure you're safe.

93
00:04:51,267 --> 00:04:52,033
Game?

94
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,200
Just say the word.
You're probably shy.

95
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:55,800
On your scooter?

96
00:04:56,333 --> 00:04:58,100
You're a reckless driver!

97
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:01,200
So if we crash, I'm the one
who's worse off, right?

98
00:05:01,367 --> 00:05:03,200
And you're so arrogant.

99
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:04,867
Like you can really
handle my stalker.

100
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,367
At this rate,
I might end up defending you.

101
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,433
Oh wow, seriously.

102
00:05:08,567 --> 00:05:10,500
See this? I worked hard
for this at the gym.

103
00:05:10,633 --> 00:05:13,700
Worked hard? You don't stand
a chance against me!

104
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:14,700
Of course not.

105
00:05:14,833 --> 00:05:16,033
I just let you win.

106
00:05:16,167 --> 00:05:17,633
- So arrogant.
- Oh...

107
00:05:17,767 --> 00:05:18,800
Really?

108
00:05:18,933 --> 00:05:20,833
- Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.
- Really?

109
00:05:20,967 --> 00:05:22,567
So you're scared after all!

110
00:05:27,433 --> 00:05:29,067
Hey.

111
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:31,800
Are you okay?

112
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:35,767
It's nothing.

113
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:38,033
I just missed laughing
like this.

114
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,000
Whenever I'm with dad,

115
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,400
this is how we tease each other.

116
00:05:42,533 --> 00:05:43,933
I just miss him.

117
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:47,467
Then call him.

118
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,533
What if he doesn't want
to talk to me?

119
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:55,467
Then apologize.

120
00:05:56,333 --> 00:05:58,867
You know, sometimes
that's all they want to hear.

121
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,467
And I'm sure...

122
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,267
your dad misses you so much too.

123
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,267
It's already late, Joey.

124
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,833
You still have school tomorrow.

125
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,300
- Come on now, okay?
- Yes, Mom.

126
00:06:27,067 --> 00:06:30,833
And you, aren't you
going to your room yet?

127
00:06:30,967 --> 00:06:32,067
I'm coming, Auntie.

128
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,033
I'll just say good night
to my best friend.

129
00:06:34,533 --> 00:06:36,200
-I'm coming.
-All right. Get some rest, okay?

130
00:06:36,333 --> 00:06:37,767
Thank you.

131
00:06:44,333 --> 00:06:45,600
Miguel...

132
00:06:45,733 --> 00:06:49,800
you shouldn't have talked back
to the Chief like that.

133
00:06:51,833 --> 00:06:54,600
Unless you really don't plan
on returning to the service,

134
00:06:54,733 --> 00:06:58,067
then that would make sense,
but I know you.

135
00:06:59,467 --> 00:07:00,667
You wouldn't just give up...

136
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:03,100
being a cop over
something like that.

137
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,433
So, Miguel?
Did you even have an alibi...

138
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:11,967
on the night Ramon died?

139
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:14,433
And you were alone.

140
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,367
Buddy, I know you.

141
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,633
I know there's a lot
you still want to say to me.

142
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,767
And I'm not forcing you.

143
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,867
I'm just waiting for you
to open up on your own.

144
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,300
Surely...

145
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:29,067
you can trust me...

146
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,267
with something like that, right?

147
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:37,433
I was with Golda.

148
00:07:38,533 --> 00:07:40,500
The woman in the video?

149
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,067
So it was true after all.

150
00:07:45,733 --> 00:07:47,067
No, that's not true.

151
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,400
She's not my woman.

152
00:07:49,367 --> 00:07:50,867
She's my informant.

153
00:07:52,633 --> 00:07:55,100
There's a drug deal
happening at her spa,

154
00:07:55,233 --> 00:07:57,400
so she knows
when the deliveries are.

155
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:02,067
The tip for our last operation
also came from her.

156
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,767
She's undocumented.

157
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,600
She's not in the system.

158
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:10,867
Her name isn't
in my reports either.

159
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:14,467
That's why I can't counter
what they're saying.

160
00:08:15,133 --> 00:08:16,867
I have no evidence.

161
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:22,100
Where is she now, that woman?

162
00:08:22,267 --> 00:08:23,333
I don't know.

163
00:08:23,467 --> 00:08:24,833
She's missing.

164
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:27,933
The people she ratted out
might be looking for her.

165
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,400
Chances are, I'm next.

166
00:08:34,833 --> 00:08:36,467
Good thing...

167
00:08:37,467 --> 00:08:39,000
my wife and child aren't here.

168
00:08:42,067 --> 00:08:44,067
I don't want them dragged
into this mess.

169
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:54,767
Joey.

170
00:08:55,233 --> 00:08:56,300
What?

171
00:08:59,033 --> 00:09:00,100
What's this?

172
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,400
Oh...

173
00:09:05,533 --> 00:09:07,267
Did you make a PowerPoint
presentation

174
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:09,400
about your feelings for me?

175
00:09:09,533 --> 00:09:10,933
You're really making me laugh.

176
00:09:11,067 --> 00:09:12,800
Wow! Wow! Amazing! Amazing!

177
00:09:12,933 --> 00:09:14,033
Maybe you have feelings for me.

178
00:09:14,167 --> 00:09:16,433
- Me?
- You're so full of yourself.

179
00:09:16,567 --> 00:09:18,167
- Whoo!
- Me, really?

180
00:09:18,833 --> 00:09:20,733
- Wow!
- No.

181
00:09:21,667 --> 00:09:23,400
That's the video you recorded.

182
00:09:25,867 --> 00:09:27,533
The one about Ramon Orbos.

183
00:09:28,367 --> 00:09:30,133
I already deleted that, right?

184
00:09:30,267 --> 00:09:31,633
When you first showed it to me,

185
00:09:31,767 --> 00:09:33,800
I sent it to myself first,

186
00:09:33,933 --> 00:09:35,700
then transferred it there.

187
00:09:35,833 --> 00:09:37,767
There are no other copies,
this is the only one left.

188
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:40,900
But, Joey...

189
00:09:41,033 --> 00:09:44,633
I think it was wrong for us to
delete that video...

190
00:09:45,967 --> 00:09:47,067
because the two of us
are the only ones who know...

191
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:49,167
what really happened to Ramon.

192
00:09:50,367 --> 00:09:52,633
All right, I'll keep it safe.

193
00:09:53,367 --> 00:09:55,067
Thank you, Peter.

194
00:10:13,867 --> 00:10:16,033
- Take this with you for lunch.
- Thank you.

195
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:19,867
You too, Peter,
eat here as well, okay?

196
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,100
Okay, I'll just finish this.

197
00:10:23,833 --> 00:10:27,000
Joey, is it dangerous
where you live?

198
00:10:27,133 --> 00:10:29,500
Why do you even
need to install CCTV?

199
00:10:30,933 --> 00:10:33,567
We need to make sure Joey
doesn't have a stalker.

200
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,000
What did you say?

201
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,033
Oh, what I meant was...

202
00:10:39,167 --> 00:10:40,567
better safe than sorry!

203
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:42,767
Let's have CCTV installed.

204
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:46,033
RS Installation CCTV service,
at your service.

205
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,767
What?

206
00:10:49,233 --> 00:10:52,867
Oh, that's just
their shop's tagline.

207
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:55,167
Oh...

208
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:57,133
- I'm going.
- All right.

209
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,233
Take care, okay? Love you.

210
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:00,800
- Oh.
- Love you, Mom.

211
00:11:06,867 --> 00:11:09,033
Go on inside, okay,
if you get hungry.

212
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,633
Okay.

213
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:57,467
Boss.

214
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:59,933
Do you know where
Major Delgado lives?

215
00:12:00,067 --> 00:12:02,200
Delgado?
You're going to interview him?

216
00:12:02,333 --> 00:12:04,633
Good luck!
Don't even try it.

217
00:12:04,767 --> 00:12:08,100
You might piss him off
and end up like me.

218
00:12:15,933 --> 00:12:16,767
I'm sorry.

219
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:18,133
It's okay.

220
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:25,433
Jay's Pro Gym...

221
00:12:27,067 --> 00:12:29,300
JPG?

222
00:12:52,733 --> 00:12:54,500
Joey!

223
00:12:55,133 --> 00:12:56,867
- Oh?
- Hey!

224
00:13:09,667 --> 00:13:11,667
Hey! You have a crush on him,
right?

225
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:12,700
What?

226
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:14,267
He's tall!

227
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,867
I just glanced
and I already like him?

228
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,333
You know what,
let's just go inside.

229
00:13:18,467 --> 00:13:21,100
Our grumpy professor
might get mad again.

230
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:22,200
Let's go.

231
00:13:22,333 --> 00:13:23,800
Same, I don't want her mad.

232
00:13:23,933 --> 00:13:27,000
But wow, he's tall.

233
00:13:27,133 --> 00:13:29,233
I wonder who that is.

234
00:13:29,367 --> 00:13:31,700
We have a lot of police
customers here, Sir.

235
00:13:31,833 --> 00:13:34,900
The owner's a former cop,
so there's a special discount.

236
00:13:35,533 --> 00:13:37,867
But we can give you
a discount too.

237
00:13:38,467 --> 00:13:39,867
No, it's fine.
Maybe next time.

238
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,633
Do you know Ramon Orbos?

239
00:13:43,567 --> 00:13:45,667
The one who was salvaged, Sir?

240
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:50,400
Do you know where
his locker is here?

241
00:13:51,067 --> 00:13:53,367
Well, Sir,
any locker can be used

242
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:55,333
as long as the member
has their own padlock.

243
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:56,700
But Sir, I remember...

244
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:57,567
This one.

245
00:13:58,400 --> 00:13:59,733
That's the one he usually used.

246
00:13:59,867 --> 00:14:01,033
That's his padlock.

247
00:14:06,033 --> 00:14:07,367
Do you...

248
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,833
have CCTV here?

249
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:10,333
It's not allowed, Sir.

250
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,733
All right, okay.
Thanks anyway.

251
00:14:13,867 --> 00:14:16,867
And let's keep this
just between us.

252
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,767
Of course, Boss Idol.

253
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:21,000
So, what now?
I'll stay here for a bit.

254
00:14:21,133 --> 00:14:22,500
- All right.
- Thank you.

255
00:16:22,067 --> 00:16:23,300
So...

256
00:16:23,433 --> 00:16:24,633
You're a mascot.

257
00:16:25,733 --> 00:16:29,467
Metropolitan State University.

258
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,733
That's so unfair, Joey.

259
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,367
What is this? I even reviewed
for the practical exam,

260
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,933
then it turns out
Prof. Grumpy isn't here.

261
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:45,100
So, are you in your studious
girl era now?

262
00:16:45,233 --> 00:16:47,600
But of course,
I got that from you.

263
00:16:47,733 --> 00:16:49,900
You know what, Joey,
let's just eat, please.

264
00:16:50,033 --> 00:16:51,533
I'm starving already.

265
00:16:51,667 --> 00:16:53,800
All right, you go ahead first,
I still have something to do.

266
00:16:53,933 --> 00:16:55,167
You're still studying?

267
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,167
Joey, what are you
talking about?

268
00:16:56,300 --> 00:16:59,300
There's nothing higher
than a one, right?

269
00:16:59,433 --> 00:17:03,333
And Joey, your parents are
already overly proud of you.

270
00:17:03,467 --> 00:17:04,567
Just go on, you go first.

271
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:06,100
I'll just follow.

272
00:17:07,033 --> 00:17:08,333
Come on.

273
00:17:08,467 --> 00:17:09,600
Really?

274
00:17:10,167 --> 00:17:11,233
I'll just follow later.

275
00:17:11,367 --> 00:17:12,833
All right then.

276
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:15,800
Take care, okay?

277
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:38,100
So, Andrew...

278
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:43,233
Looks like your sibling invited
you to the party too.

279
00:17:43,367 --> 00:17:47,067
Actually, I didn't know there
was a party, Mom.

280
00:17:48,867 --> 00:17:51,200
I already told your sibling...

281
00:17:51,333 --> 00:17:54,933
that I don't want strangers
coming here.

282
00:17:57,467 --> 00:17:58,467
But they said...

283
00:17:59,467 --> 00:18:01,533
They'll just stay in the garden.

284
00:18:01,667 --> 00:18:04,000
But you know, what if...

285
00:18:04,133 --> 00:18:06,233
What if someone sneaks in?

286
00:18:06,367 --> 00:18:09,300
What if someone gets inside
the house? What then?

287
00:18:09,433 --> 00:18:12,967
What if someone tries
to kill me again, Andrew?

288
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,167
Ma'am...

289
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:16,233
Ma'am, please calm down.

290
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:21,500
Mom...

291
00:18:22,167 --> 00:18:23,967
I understand you.

292
00:18:25,067 --> 00:18:28,300
I promise you,
nobody can hurt you.

293
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
As long as I am here,

294
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:35,600
I will protect you
at all costs.

295
00:18:35,733 --> 00:18:38,800
And this compound is secured.

296
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:43,900
Sir, ma'am will be able
to sleep in a while.

297
00:18:44,033 --> 00:18:45,833
I'll leave the two of you
for now.

298
00:18:45,967 --> 00:18:46,967
Okay, thank you.

299
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:57,867
- Mom...
- What?

300
00:18:59,933 --> 00:19:03,233
The reason why I'm here
is because...

301
00:19:03,367 --> 00:19:04,867
I'm working on something.

302
00:19:05,767 --> 00:19:06,867
Oh.

303
00:19:12,533 --> 00:19:15,033
I'm still feeling
that this could be...

304
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:17,300
a big exposé,

305
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:20,467
especially if I find out,

306
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:23,533
if I figure out
what's written here.

307
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:54,000
Hello?

308
00:19:54,133 --> 00:19:55,567
Dad, are you okay?

309
00:19:58,167 --> 00:19:59,033
Joey...

310
00:20:01,233 --> 00:20:02,233
So it's you.

311
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,200
Why did you call?

312
00:20:04,733 --> 00:20:07,033
Why do you sound drunk?
Didn't you go to work?

313
00:20:09,233 --> 00:20:10,667
Oh, I'm just on vacation.

314
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,967
Vacation? Why?

315
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:14,600
<i> Just tired from work.</i>

316
00:20:15,333 --> 00:20:17,167
And I still have some leave.

317
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:19,833
Dad, please don't lie anymore.

318
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:24,167
If this is about mom and me,

319
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,633
<i> I'm really sorry, Dad.</i>

320
00:20:27,667 --> 00:20:30,933
I was just shocked
by what happened.

321
00:20:31,067 --> 00:20:33,333
I was really confused, but...

322
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:35,833
<i>I really shouldn't
have doubted you.</i>

323
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,700
So I'm sorry, Dad.

324
00:20:38,367 --> 00:20:39,933
<i>Joey, you didn't do
anything wrong.</i>

325
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:41,867
There's just an issue
at the office,

326
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,900
that's why I haven't been able
to visit you and your mom.

327
00:20:46,833 --> 00:20:48,200
What issue, Dad?

328
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:50,533
Oh, it's nothing...

329
00:20:50,967 --> 00:20:51,967
I can handle this.

330
00:20:54,167 --> 00:20:56,900
Dad, please don't keep secrets
from me anymore.

331
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:01,300
You see, you've had so many
secrets from Mom and me,

332
00:21:01,433 --> 00:21:03,167
and that's why
we keep having problems.

333
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,367
Come on, Dad.

334
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,633
What's the problem?

335
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:10,100
I'm under investigation for...

336
00:21:11,133 --> 00:21:13,967
for the death of Staff Sergeant
Ramon Orbos.

337
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:15,000
What?

338
00:21:22,267 --> 00:21:24,400
But I had nothing to do
with that.

339
00:21:24,533 --> 00:21:25,967
Of course, Dad!

340
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:27,100
That's impossible.

341
00:21:27,233 --> 00:21:29,267
I know you didn't do it.

342
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:31,067
Thank you for trusting me.

343
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:32,900
Dad, I don't just
believe you blindly.

344
00:21:33,033 --> 00:21:34,167
I know the truth.

345
00:21:34,433 --> 00:21:35,533
What is it?

346
00:21:35,667 --> 00:21:37,367
Let's just meet now.

347
00:21:37,633 --> 00:21:39,467
I will give you something
that can help you.

348
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:52,967
Relax.

349
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:54,233
I'm...
I'm Jin Ho.

350
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:56,033
- I'll explain everything.
- You think I don't know?

351
00:21:56,167 --> 00:21:58,067
You've been following me
since last night!

352
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:01,033
I have a small gathering
outside with some sponsors.

353
00:22:01,367 --> 00:22:02,600
Do you know my daugther,

354
00:22:02,733 --> 00:22:03,933
Joey Delgado?

355
00:22:04,067 --> 00:22:06,433
She said she'd wait
for you here,

356
00:22:06,567 --> 00:22:07,633
but she suddenly left.

357
00:22:07,767 --> 00:22:09,867
You know you can always rely
on me to help you, right?

358
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,067
Don't worry, Brother.

359
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:13,167
If ever I need your help,
you're the one I'll go to.

360
00:22:13,300 --> 00:22:15,000
She went that way,
toward the market.

361
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,433
- You're cornered!
- Who are you?

362
00:22:16,567 --> 00:22:18,100
Are you with the one
who shot my mother?

363
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:20,567
I won't let anyone
hurt my family again.

364
00:22:20,700 --> 00:22:22,300
So you do know each other?

365
00:22:25,533 --> 00:22:28,000
Joey...
